But lojban, unlike English, has a culture of not using more specific a word
than necessary to get meaning across, and since I expect that if, suddenly,
a company emerged that depended on relativistic speeds to solve the same
problem that modern cryonics does, I don't expect the words used to
describe the processes would be different (people are lazy and don't care
about details), but suddenly, cold is not just incidental but incorrect.

